# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale el
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as morning [04:00, 12:00) (CLDR
# morning1+morning2 collapsed into chronologia's four-band model).
# Surface: πρωί (proï), the neuter noun for "morning"; used bare as an
# adverb ("in the morning") and after the article ("το πρωί").
# Source: Wiktionary, "πρωί" (noun, gender "n")
# https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/πρωί
# Gender confirms the neuter accusative article "το" (Wiktionary, "το",
# neuter nominative/accusative singular of "ο":
# https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/το).
πρωί
